{"id":28106,"slug":"the-canterbury-tales","title":"The Canterbury Tales","year":1972,"country":"Italy","duration":111,"spine":633,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/28106-the-canterbury-tales","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/65d5e2b831a35d5d9834dc81f2cdf43d/q4Zt7iiONKEVKdkAQb9yvCDgXOT8BG_large.jpg","description":"Eight of Geoffrey Chaucer’s lusty tales come to life on-screen in Pier Paolo Pasolini’s gutsy and delirious The Canterbury Tales, which was shot in England and offers a remarkably earthy re-creation of the medieval era. From the story of a nobleman struck blind after marrying a much younger and promiscuous bride to a climactic trip to a hell populated by friars and demons (surely one of the most outrageously conceived and realized sequences ever committed to film), this is an endlessly imaginative work of merry blasphemy, framed by Pasolini’s portrayal of Chaucer himself. ","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Pier Paolo Pasolini","slug":"pier-paolo-pasolini"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Hugh Griffith","role":"Sir January","slug":"hugh-griffith"},{"actor":"Laura Betti","role":"Wife of Bath","slug":"laura-betti"},{"actor":"Ninetto Davoli","role":"Peterkin","slug":"ninetto-davoli"},{"actor":"Franco Citti","role":"Devil","slug":"franco-citti"},{"actor":"Josephine Chaplin","role":"May","slug":"josephine-chaplin"},{"actor":"Alan Webb","role":"Old man","slug":"alan-webb"},{"actor":"Pier Paolo Pasolini","role":"Geoffrey Chaucer","slug":"pier-paolo-pasolini"},{"actor":"J. P. Van Dyne","role":"Cook","slug":"j-p-van-dyne"},{"actor":"Vernon Dobtcheff","role":"Franklin","slug":"vernon-dobtcheff"},{"actor":"Adrian Street","role":"Fighter","slug":"adrian-street"},{"actor":"Ot","role":"Chief witch-hunter","slug":"ot"},{"actor":"Derek Deadmin","role":"Pardoner","slug":"derek-deadmin"},{"actor":"Nicholas Smith","role":"Friar","slug":"nicholas-smith"},{"actor":"Goerge B. Datch","role":"Host of the tabard","slug":"goerge-b-datch"},{"actor":"Pet